---
title: How to read these docs
summary: The two reading orders (top-down and bottom-up), the design-decision records, and the plain-text versions of every page for language models.
order: 3
---

These docs are organized so you can come at skoro from either end.

## Two reading orders

**The [Guide](../../guide/) is top-down.** It starts from what a user writes: a model, a
distribution, a call to evaluate a density or build a solver step. It explains the machinery only
as far as that use needs. Read it if you want to *use* skoro, or to judge quickly whether it fits
your problem.

**[Concepts](../../concepts/) is bottom-up.** It builds skoro one crate at a time in dependency
order: tensors, then differentiable operations, then manifolds, the graph, the compiler, the model
facade, and the distributions and estimators on top. Each page relies only on the pages before it.
Read it if you want to *extend* skoro (a new operation, manifold, or distribution) or to review
its internals.

The two tracks link to each other where they meet. Neither repeats the
[Design decisions](../../design/), which record *why* things are the way they are, each as
context, decision, consequences, and alternatives considered.

## Conventions

> [!NOTE]
> A note adds context you can skip.

> [!WARNING]
> A warning marks a mistake that fails silently: the result looks right and isn't.

> [!DECISION]
> A design decision summarizes one of the records in [Design decisions](../../design/).

Code blocks with a file name above them are quoted verbatim from the repository at build time, so
they always match the source. Click the file name to open it on GitHub.

Math uses the notation on the [Notation](../../reference/notation/) page. A page's own
macros are listed in its frontmatter, and the Markdown version of the page shows them.

## For language models

Every page has a plain Markdown version: add `.md` to its URL, or follow "View as Markdown" at the
foot of the page. Two indexes follow the [llms.txt](https://llmstxt.org) convention:

- [`/llms.txt`](../../llms.txt): an index of every page with a one-line summary.
- [`/llms-full.txt`](../../llms-full.txt): every page concatenated in reading order, with quoted code
  inlined.
